[I] Control pulseaudio volume from the shell or mapped to keyboard shortcuts

[T] pulseaudio-ctl is a simple Bash script to control PulseAudio volume and
[T] mute state of outputs and inputs from the shell, without the ALSA
[T] utilities. Its commands are meant to be mapped to keyboard shortcuts in
[T] a desktop environment or window manager, with optional notifications
[T] configured in ~/.config/pulseaudio-ctl/config.

[U] https://github.com/graysky2/pulseaudio-ctl

